Search applications by name, generic name and keyword

The desktop applications provider fuzzy-matched the Exec line, the Comment
and the keywords joined into one string. On NixOS the Exec line is usually
a /nix/store path, so "nix" or "store" listed most applications, and an
argument such as steam://rungameid matched "set". Long comments and the
joined keyword list matched short queries across unrelated words: "fire"
found a contact book through "friends,address book". Match the name, an
action's application, the generic name and each keyword on its own, with
upstream's penalties for those fields.

A match on another field also replaced the subtext, the generic name, with
the field it matched, such as the raw keyword list. Keep the generic name
(an action's application name) as the subtext, so that a launcher can show
what an application is beneath its name, and leave it empty when it only
repeats the name ("Clocks", "Clocks").

